    "learningOutcome": "Students connect linear functions to real-world situations.",
    "type": "Knowledge",
    "text": "Function notation can be used to represent\n• a function symbolically, e.g., f(x) = 2x + 3\n• the output value for a given input value, e.g., if the input value x = 3,\nf(3) = 9",
    "sourcePage": 9,
